+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4c47c68-de5c-5236-b155-78a447eb8332" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338171} :answer-field/id #uuid "7718debd-009e-52ad-b486-a85853f1ee0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338482}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81c6457c-f4fd-58e1-87c0-0244bbebd614" :question/math-academy-id "q-70898" :question/problem "![](images/88/887895a47cf6ce3a6f109f754ef0c46eecaa6d68763baf3a696008e014d231af.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-2,-3)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=8.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={8}^{2} \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087656 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087464 :question/id #uuid "e2d2147e-98df-54df-a271-4c5dff362a96" :question/math-academy-id "e-3226" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x-2)^2 + (y+4)^2 = 9?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y+4)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-(-4))^{2} & ={3}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a = 2,$ $b = - 4,$ and $r = 3.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,-4)$ and its radius is $3.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0576cbfe-64f6-5bc3-a016-f311431b8cc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,3)$ and radius is $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342291} {:answer/id #uuid "2d02910a-922e-5c4c-b5fc-7dd9508107d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-2,-3)$ and radius is $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342614} {:answer/id #uuid "30c13b16-79f8-5389-b2ee-a0eb671325c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342645} {:answer/id #uuid "bc241e1f-2741-5d91-8f59-ef85f94eac0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-2,-3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343891} {:answer/id #uuid "c972847a-26b8-5b15-aa4d-ff0fb36da0a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c972847a-26b8-5b15-aa4d-ff0fb36da0a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344005} :answer-field/id #uuid "89edcb63-a33b-5de5-ba63-aeca3edd3169" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344735}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c280c3e5-8a01-5bfb-b585-89deed38b8eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-7521" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=6?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =6 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{6})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=2,$ $b=3,$ and $r=\\sqrt{6}.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,3)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{6}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83750412-13d3-53b5-b710-5024a1954edd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,-1)$ and radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086527} {:answer/id #uuid "933eca4a-b650-5a3a-883c-f905c2389a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,-1)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086528} {:answer/id #uuid "95761f1a-a3e0-5727-9225-0803ad54c6b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5, 1)$ and radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086529} {:answer/id #uuid "05806bc8-cd02-5c0b-bf54-4f7466a6c0f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5, 1)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086530} {:answer/id #uuid "12c0ca05-f49d-5fa0-b7df-8a6667d46198" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,-1)$ and radius is $4^{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086531}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7264ccff-1242-5bcf-aa59-50d9a42715cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086526}] :question/id #uuid "0b82b51c-240a-56bc-959f-8619bdcbeea5" :question/math-academy-id "q-7527" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x + 5)^{2} + (y + 1)^{2} = 4$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253303 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2155b67f-cc1d-5498-baae-1a55b610aaeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-