936} {:answer/id #uuid "51ebda4a-c6ab-56ec-a85d-515c28547d71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251224} {:answer/id #uuid "9cde4a0d-d36b-53dd-9c07-256ac68ea24e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251906} {:answer/id #uuid "c3b65520-eb87-5289-bc62-41aa3b67fb30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252285} {:answer/id #uuid "df53c346-071e-5d55-b02f-a149afdcd833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df53c346-071e-5d55-b02f-a149afdcd833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252522} :answer-field/id #uuid "311dd4be-59af-5907-99cb-162e30c5bc61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252890}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93ab0f69-1e36-5855-80b5-7cee6cddd602" :question/math-academy-id "q-117102" :question/problem "![](images/af/afd2f435a60fbb5a0f0f83c5f8965a74ca107d1ed4b14d03401f7966a323d2f1.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(2,4)$ and $(2,0)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(2,4)$ and $Y(2,0),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(4-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, we can find the center using the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{2+2}{2},\\frac{4+0}{2})=(2,2)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2$ and center $(a,b)=(2,2),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253307 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23dbf520-5c3b-5b0b-ba2f-9f13812d437b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250862} {:answer/id #uuid "bd2c3273-1427-5200-b8fa-ae62dd0254b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252224} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d74c25-4afb-5a05-86ec-741a51b80fe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252690} {:answer/id #uuid "f4f229e0-e36c-5d89-bfa3-eb4e80db5b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252700} {:answer/id #uuid "fb945b04-2597-5034-872d-2f63ecdf08d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23dbf520-5c3b-5b0b-ba2f-9f13812d437b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250862} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ee3ff0f-0ad3-57b0-80be-ce3303f10b7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253051}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e7556293-0fd9-5aac-b946-74962289d2c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-117103" :question/problem "![](images/08/08653e0cdc9bb404bd7ef193dfc9f1b5c0884002e83dd72cbcbda5779a2363a1.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(2,-1)$ and $(2,1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(2,-1)$ and $Y(2,1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(-1-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, we can find the center using the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{2+2}{2},\\frac{-1+1}{2})=(2,0)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=1$ and center $(a,b)=(2,0),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={1}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1449a778-d0cd-54af-b254-ed3e6cf1e350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250729} {:answer/id #uuid "210a0d60-0ad2-5c82-bbdf-57fa4f773dd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250833} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbdbf00-5f32-5f31-b62b-8082aac14eb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251080} {:answer/id #uuid "9aa1cebc-2118-57ee-afa4-b243d9a8d486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251881} {:answer/id #uuid "c79d3915-b972-5b9e-9dbd-ac4105903344" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c79d3915-b972-5b9e-9dbd-ac4105903344" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252320} :answer-field/id #uuid "8058d059-e858-5260-9048-73a64f45f512" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253024}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7713e957-0cbe-5d3f-93d1-81e2b678b8a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-117105" :question/problem "![](images/05/0598fca48db1dbfb0cacadcf2ffb5cd987fc4e922fe85585849763fedac1f28e.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-3,0)$ and $(1,-2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-3,0)$ and $Y(1,-2),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-3-1)^{2}+(0-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-3+1}{2},\\frac{0-2}{2})=(-1,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and center $(a,b)=(-1,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27146995-40b8-5fb9-a436-de880c16f96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250890} {:answer/id #uuid "3d3b83a1-785f-569a-9e04-1f4d911a200b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251061} {:answer/id #uuid "6e015f74-e5e1-5e7d-8695-c6dc5c93e9ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251454} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8ee6e0-b5ff-59bc-82f8-2de8c7c6342b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251762} {:answer/id #uuid "b43bb4a8-cb77-5ae2-870d-f55b9e5f7c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b43bb4a8-cb77-5ae2-870d-f55b9e5f7c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252136} :answer-field/id #uuid "94017d7f-a209-5ab8-99c1-91d78574ffbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253064}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6610e1ab-73a7-5f4a-8c57-8d6e77beff9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-117106" :question/problem "![](images/0a/0a0820b21672bbf16d2fdb35d708aefc4129fdc81c7594b55af3bd2ef5b8fc0f.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-2,0)$ and $(0,2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-2,0)$ and $Y(0,2),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-2-0)^{2}+(0-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-2+0}{2},\\frac{0+2}{2})=(-1,1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{2}$ and center $(a,b)=(-1,1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34b1554c-96e1-5f34-bd7d-39439e7d2d90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250994} {:answer/id #uuid "3e0c96c8-b6f3-508c-bbce-383fbffc5d73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251069} {:answer/id #uuid "71463607-983f-5491-bdcc-71080d1290aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251480} {:answer/id #uuid "78ba35b2-ca4d-559a-9e58-c33761c27a13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251553} {:answer/id #uuid "dbfbf876-ab7e-5bb9-b30b-9654f0019146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34b1554c-96e1-5f34-bd7d-39439e7d2d90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250994} :answer-field/id #uuid "233384c8-214c-54f0-a58a-ee2651d7fa9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252869}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b6f2966b-20a6-5c34-af5a-1e6c31f128aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-117107" :question/problem "![](images/7f/7f1573d17cb9a603727b644da6598355875b0be4b8c43a382e562155cb7a095c.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-1,-3)$ and $(3,1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-1,-3)$ and $Y(3,1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-1-3)^{2}+(-3-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{2}=2\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-1+3}{2},\\frac{-3+1}{2})=(1,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2\\sqrt{2}$ and center $(a,b)=(1,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "301aa6a7-5ee2-5a20-9033-4674a143461b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336492} {:answer/id #uuid "64b4c7ae-6592-5435-9dcf-3efafb11647a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336934} {:answer/id #uuid "7faacc68-2956-5fc6-9e73-4fc524688331" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}-(y+3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337190} {:answer/id #uuid "8864933a-7a46-5b44-8a98-d9f22b098b5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337262} {:answer/id #uuid "ed738468-0ab1-5dc7-96f4-55c16f6a1c9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64b4c7ae-6592-5435-9dcf-3efafb11647a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336934} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6d043a5-1717-5a07-aecc-41e08ef6bda7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338587}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ffdebd9-641e-5fc7-a83b-a3474a188cc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-70987" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b6a4e9a8f4a1c6dcaaad453b843896f3fc56ae22a37d481dcb4cfe54cc53361d.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(7,3)$ and $(-1,3)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is  \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(7,3)$ and $Y(-1,3),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(7-(-1))}^{2}+{(3-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{7+(-1)}{2},\\frac{3+3}{2})=(3,3)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=4$ and center $(a,b)=(3,3),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e4a49e-453f-5b68-98b1-7a31adb93775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}-{y}^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336038} {:answer/id #uuid "450d803a-0dda-576f-ae85-76770d27f4a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336677} {:answer/id #uuid "7ee14867-8540-55f0-b7a0-7100bebee222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337181} {:answer/id #uuid "87685e0e-a82f-5609-beee-7cd2ee774d09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+{y}^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337255} {:answer/id #uuid "adc4df30-8770-5d9e-9c11-b2f992c2a043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ee14867-8540-55f0-b7a0-7100bebee222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337181} :answer-field/id #uuid "0625c9ee-953d-5a19-becb-0ce059539921" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338285}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4b08908d-2189-5c82-98e7-76da156bba41" :question/math-academy-id "q-70990" :question/problem "![](images/a6/a6a21dbf4785a270a0ae03066df1f92df73974532f9a75aa8e470cef42ea5e14.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-3,2)$ and $(3,4)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is  \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-3,2)$ and $Y(3,4),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(-3-3)}^{2}+{(2-4)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 10} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{2}=\\sqrt{10}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-3+3}{2},\\frac{2+4}{2})=(0,3)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and center $(a,b)=(0,3),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{10})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087686 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087433 :question/id #uuid "4f0593d8-bce5-5c73-aedd-ffe0faf15a59" :question/math-academy-id "e-14364" :question/problem "The lines $y=cx+7$ and $y=5x-3$ are parallel. What is the value of $c$?" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nBoth lines are in slope-intercept form, so we can pick out the slope of each equation by looking at the $x$-coefficient.\n\n- The slope of the line $y=cx+7$ is $c$.\n- The slope of the line $y=5x-3$ is $5$.\n\nBecause the slopes must be the same, we must have $c=5$."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "353a2fb8-5677-5047-8f39-595f43d9eeb9" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "c12cfecd-6908-57f1-91b4-ad6618d6b44c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085140}] :question/id #uuid "8abba1b4-cf74-5469-9ad3-fd07f923a0f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-215719" :question/problem "The lines $y =-7x + 5$ and $y = mx + 2$ are parallel. What is the value of $m$?$m =$\n{{field-1}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088073 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "51594eb3-a520-5a77-a55d-36ea7b41a396" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085141}] :question/id #uuid "570f0d0a-a716-58d6-9635-7e7137caf659" :question/math-academy-id "q-215726" :question/problem "The lines $y =-\\frac{1}{8}x - 4$ and $y = mx + 6$ are parallel. What is the value of $m$?$m =$\n{{field-1}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088176 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb95632f-ccbf-5d8f-8ed1-2b2d0954659a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085711} {:answer/id #uuid "c49f151f-9fbc-5315-8cfe-17182c6e7632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085712} {:answer/id #uuid "0c440183-193f-5d9b-828a-44233e8fa0eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085713} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5d8556-a95d-533a-999f-c615170feaa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085714} {:answer/id #uuid "784e60a9-33b8-5b95-af91-5f0539e6abae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085715}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ae270df8-9bf6-5641-82b1-ee2708e40405" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085710}] :question/id #uuid "9944ab8b-e161-5e8d-b3cc-b5e68c5e2162" :question/math-academy-id "q-44314" :question/problem "The lines $y = 2x + 3$ and $y = mx + 9$ are parallel. The value of $m =$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parallel Lines Given in Slope-Intercept Form"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087687 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087434 :question/id #uuid "b2f31785-e173-518c-a1fd-b069e0834b2a" :question/math-academy-id "e-14367" :question/problem "Which of the following lines is parallel to $12x - y=3$?\n\n1. $y=4x-8$\n2. $y=12x+1$\n3. $y=3x-12$" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of the line $12x-y=3$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12x - y &= 3 \\\\\n- y &= -12x + 3 \\\\\ny &= 12x - 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $12$.\n\nFrom the given options, the only line that has a slope of $12$ is\n\n$$\ny = 12x+1\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5bf8c8b-64f1-5552-a59e-78eef021c122" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6bf01d9-1387-514b-afb5-fde88dafcb9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{3}{2}x + 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084615} {:answer/id #uuid "1e7fa38f-3d7a-58ce-b27f-e3d665aba389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{9}{4}x + \\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084616} {:answer/id #uuid "25180595-bbf1-583a-9a44-97d13f692586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 6x + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084617} {:answer/id #uuid "38aee078-8100-5d7d-9eb6-406ce83f2e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{2}{3}x - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084618} {:answer/id #uuid "5977f454-540b-54e7-8f16-ad456776a01b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/m